	/**
	 * Sql Server only supports online index operations on some editions (e.g. Enterprise, Developer).  Rather
	 * than detect the edition, we wrap the online operation in a TRY/CATCH block so that when the server does
	 * not support ONLINE, we fall back to the table-locking variant.
	 * <p>
	 * Note that we use {@code EXEC()} in the TRY branch so that the resulting error severity is low enough for
	 * the CATCH branch to handle it.
	 *
	 * @param theSql the bare create/drop index statement (without the {@code WITH (ONLINE = ON)} clause)
	 * @return the TRY/CATCH wrapped statement
